  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "source": [
    "# # Adult Income Classification\n",
    "## Logistic Regression vs Decision Tree vs Random Forest vs SVM vs GaussianNB\n",
    "\n",
    "**Task:** Predict `income` (>50K vs <=50K) from 1994 US Census features.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Dataset:** UCI Adult / OpenML `adult` version 2 (48,842 rows)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.datasets import fetch_openml\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split, StratifiedKFold, cross_val_score\n",
    "from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\n",
    "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
    "from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler, OneHotEncoder\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
    "from sklearn.tree import DecisionTreeClassifier\n",
    "from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\n",
    "from sklearn.svm import LinearSVC\n",
    "from sklearn.naive_bayes import GaussianNB\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import (
",
    "    classification_report, confusion_matrix, ConfusionMatrixDisplay,\n",
    "    f1_score, roc_auc_score, accuracy_score\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Official UCI Adult via OpenML (same data as Hugging Face scikit-learn/adult-census-income)\n",
    "adult = fetch_openml(name=\"adult\", version=2, as_frame=True, parser=\"auto\")\n",
    "df = adult.frame.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Shape:\", df.shape)\n",
    "print(\"\\nColumns:\", df.columns.tolist())\n",
    "print(\"\\nDtypes:\\n\", df.dtypes)\n",
    "df.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Target distribution:\")\n",
    "print(df[\"class\"].value_counts())\n",
    "print(\"\\nProportions:\")\n",
    "print(df[\"class\"].value_counts(normalize=True).round(3))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nMissing values:\")\n",
    "print(df.isna().sum()[df.isna().sum() > 0])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nNumeric summary:\")\n",
    "display(df.describe())\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nCategorical unique counts:\")\n",
    "for c in df.select_dtypes(include=[\"category\", \"object\"]).columns:\n",
    "    print(f\"  {c:20s} {df[c].nunique()}")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "source": [
    "~76% <=50K, ~24% >50K → mild imbalance. Accuracy alone will look good if you always predict <=50K. Track F1 on >50K and ROC-AUC.\n",
    "Missing: workclass, occupation, native-country. Do not drop 2–3k rows blindly if you can impute.\n",
    "education and education-num are the same information (text vs ordinal). Drop one later to avoid redundancy.\n",
    "fnlwgt is a census sampling weight, not a personal attribute. Often dropped for this task."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df_clean = df.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Target: 1 = >50K (the class we care about)\n",
    "df_clean[\"income\"] = (df_clean[\"class\"].astype(str).str.strip() == \">50K\").astype(int)\n",
    "df_clean = df_clean.drop(columns=[\"class\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Drop redundant / non-predictive columns\n",
    "drop_cols = [\"fnlwgt\", \"education\"]   # keep education-num\n",
    "df_clean = df_clean.drop(columns=drop_cols)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"After cleaning:\", df_clean.shape)\n",
    "print(df_clean[\"income\"].value_counts(normalize=True).round(3))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "TARGET = \"income\"\n",
    "y = df_clean[TARGET]\n",
    "X = df_clean.drop(columns=[TARGET])\n",
    "\n",
    "numeric_features = X.select_dtypes(include=[\"int64\", \"float64\", \"int32\", \"float32\"]).columns.tolist()\n",
    "categorical_features = X.select_dtypes(include=[\"object\", \"category\"]).columns.tolist()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Numeric:\", numeric_features)\n",
    "print(\"Categorical:\", categorical_features)\n",
    "\n",
    "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
    "    X, y, test_size=0.2, stratify=y, random_state=42\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(\"Train:\", X_train.shape, \"Test:\", X_test.shape)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "numeric_pipe = Pipeline(steps=[\n",
    "    (\"imputer\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"median\")),\n",
    "    (\"scaler\", StandardScaler()),\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "categorical_pipe = Pipeline(steps=[\n",
    "    (\"imputer\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"most_frequent\")),\n",
    "    (\"onehot\", OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown=\"ignore\", sparse_output=False)),\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "preprocessor = ColumnTransformer(\n",
    "    transformers=[\n",
    "        (\"num\", numeric_pipe, numeric_features),\n",
    "        (\"cat\", categorical_pipe, categorical_features),\n",
    "    ]\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "source": [
    "Concepts:\n",
    "\n",
    "Pipeline + ColumnTransformer = production pattern. Same transforms on train and test.\n",
    "Impute + encode after split, fit only on train → no leakage.\n",
    "Trees don’t need scaling, but one shared preprocessor keeps comparison fair.\n",
    "One-hot is correct for unordered cats (occupation, workclass). education-num stays numeric."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "models = {\n",
    "    \"Logistic Regression\": LogisticRegression(max_iter=2000, class_weight=\"balanced\", random_state=42),\n",
    "    \"Decision Tree\": DecisionTreeClassifier(max_depth=8, class_weight=\"balanced\", random_state=42),\n",
    "    \"Random Forest\": RandomForestClassifier(\n",
    "        n_estimators=150, max_depth=16, n_jobs=-1, class_weight=\"balanced\", random_state=42\n",
    "    ),\n",
    "    \"Linear SVM\": LinearSVC(class_weight=\"balanced\", random_state=42, max_iter=2000),\n",
    "    \"GaussianNB\": GaussianNB(),\n",
    "}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "source": [
    "train predict metrics"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "cv = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=42)\n",
    "rows = []\n",
    "preds = {}\n",
    "\n",
    "for name, clf in models.items():\n",
    "    pipe = Pipeline([\n",
    "        (\"prep\", preprocessor),\n",
    "        (\"model\", clf),\n",
    "    ])\n",
    "\n",
    "    pipe.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "    y_pred = pipe.predict(X_test)\n",
    "    preds[name] = y_pred\n",
    "\n",
    "    # scores / probabilities for AUC\n",
    "    if hasattr(pipe.named_steps[\"model\"], \"predict_proba\"):\n",
    "        y_score = pipe.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]\n",
    "    elif hasattr(pipe.named_steps[\"model\"], \"decision_function\"):\n",
    "        y_score = pipe.decision_function(X_test)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        y_score = y_pred\n",
    "\n",
    "    f1 = f1_score(y_test, y_pred)\n",
    "    auc = roc_auc_score(y_test, y_score)\n",
    "    acc = accuracy_score(y_test, y_pred)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # CV on train\n",
    "    cv_f1 = cross_val_score(pipe, X_train, y_train, cv=cv, scoring=\"f1\", n_jobs=-1)\n",
    "\n",
    "    rows.append({\n",
    "        \"Model\": name,\n",
    "        \"Test Acc\": round(acc, 3),\n",
    "        \"Test F1\": round(f1, 3),\n",
    "        \"Test AUC\": round(auc, 3),\n",
    "        \"CV F1 mean\": round(cv_f1.mean(), 3),\n",
    "        \"CV F1 std\": round(cv_f1.std(), 3),\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "results = pd.DataFrame(rows).sort_values(\"Test AUC\", ascending=False)\n",
    "print(results.to_string(index=False))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 3, figsize=(14, 8))\n",
    "axes = axes.ravel()\n",
    "\n",
    "for i, (name, y_pred) in enumerate(preds.items()):\n",
    "    cm = confusion_matrix(y_test, y_pred)\n",
    "    ConfusionMatrixDisplay(cm, display_labels=[\"<=50K\", \">50K\"]).plot(\n",
    "        ax=axes[i], cmap=\"Blues\", colorbar=False\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    axes[i].set_title(name)\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[-1].axis(\"off\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "source": [
    "## Results\n",
    "\n",
    "- Dataset: UCI Adult (48,842 rows). Target = income >50K (~24%).\n",
    "- Cleaning: dropped `fnlwgt` and `education` (kept `education-num`); median impute + scale for numeric; most-frequent + one-hot for categoricals; fit preprocessor on train only.\n",
    "- Best model: Random Forest (CV F1 0.689, ROC-AUC 0.915). Lowest CV variance.\n",
    "- Single tree (depth 8) almost matches logistic regression; forest still wins by reducing variance.\n",
    "- LR and Linear SVM are close linear baselines (~0.90 AUC). Good sanity check that the problem is not only non-linear.\n",
    "- GaussianNB failed after one-hot (independence + Gaussian assumptions). Treat as a weak baseline, not a contender.\n",
    "- `class_weight='balanced'` bought high recall on >50K (~0.85) at the cost of precision (~0.56). Accuracy (~0.81) is only modestly above the majority baseline."
   ]
  }
 ]
}
